# Font binaries recovered from the fixtures. Regenerate with:
#   for f in fixtures/gdl/*.gdl; do python -m gdl.fonts "$f" gdl/fonts/; done
#
# Ignored per file rather than as a class: the nine files do not share a
# license. Open Sans is Apache 2.0 and declares it in its own name table, so it
# is tracked. Arial and Arial Black are retail Monotype faces, Forma DJR Display
# is a retail typeface, and the Extron and Crestron icon fonts carry no license
# grant at all. gdl/fonts/README.md has the per-file detail, read from each font
# rather than assumed.
#
# This ignore does not keep the bytes out of git - every face is embedded in the
# tracked .gdl fixtures and is recoverable from them exactly. It prevents a
# second, more conveniently redistributable copy, nothing more.
#
# Without the untracked faces the harness does not degrade, it stops: face()
# raises LookupError on the first one it cannot resolve.
gdl/fonts/*
!gdl/fonts/README.md
!gdl/fonts/LICENSE-OpenSans.txt
!gdl/fonts/opensans-regular.ttf
!gdl/fonts/opensans-light.ttf

# Scratch output: extracted ProjectGCP, repacked .gdl, authored results.
out/

# Built viewer artifacts (regenerate with gdl.data + viewer/build_viewer.py).
panel-data.json
panel-atlas.html

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# C:\gdlwork had its own out/ directory; archive it like everything else there.
!/archive/**/out/

# Extron's installed template library, copied here so the tests that read it
# need nothing on C:. Reinstallable with GUI Designer and ~470 MB, so it stays
# on disk but is not pushed; vendor/MANIFEST.md records exactly what belongs.
/vendor/*
!/vendor/README.md
!/vendor/MANIFEST.md
